Based on the SceneDesignerAgent's sandbox report, I have all the information needed to design the milestone for the "mine redstone_block" task.

**Key details from the scene:**
- The redstone block is placed at spawn-relative position `~5 ~1 ~7` (i.e., offset [5, 1, 7] from spawn)
- The player has an iron pickaxe (sufficient to mine redstone blocks)
- Mining a redstone block drops **redstone dust** (the item "redstone"), not the block itself, unless the pickaxe has Silk Touch
- Wait — actually, mining a `redstone_block` (the solid red block made from 9 redstone dust) with any pickaxe drops the block itself as an item called `redstone_block`

The task is "mine redstone_block" — when a player mines a redstone_block with an iron pickaxe, it drops `redstone_block` as an item that goes into inventory.

